      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AWESOME FORCE (4) gets the nod on the strength of two solid Ascot runs in stronger company. He was fifth in a 1MW last start after beginning slowly and being restrained, and his prior BM66+ sixth, beaten two and a half lengths reads well for a BM44+. SIDE SHOW (2) is the main danger after a Collie BM56+ third where he was steadied near the 600m, and his Northam CL3 win over Vancouver Storm shows he is holding form, he just has to stretch to 1920m now. RARE ROCK (8) drops out of a Saturday 1MW and had excuses when fourth in a Mdn at this track two back, so he has some claims if he finishes off better. SAUCISSON (6) has the track-and-trip profile, with one win and one placing from two starts at this distance. He can bounce back returning to a more suitable race. TIFF'S LAD (1) can improve on just a fair effort last time as this shapes as an easier race.",
